# Generated ts-rs bindings are written with LF (issue #359). Pin them to LF so
# the CI drift gate (`git diff --exit-code src/types/generated`) never trips on
# a CRLF/LF mismatch on Windows runners where core.autocrlf may be enabled.
# The harness catalog JSON snapshot (ADR-0037) is emitted by the same cargo
# test pass and must stay LF for the same reason.
# ts-rs also leaves a trailing space after a field that is followed by a doc
# comment. Regenerated output must not be hand-edited, so `git diff --check`
# (the harness whitespace gate) skips trailing-space errors for these files.
src/types/generated/*.ts text eol=lf whitespace=-trailing-space
src/types/generated/*.json text eol=lf
# Fuzz corpus seeds are exact byte streams: CRLF line endings, NUL bytes,
# invalid UTF-8, and at least one header value whose trailing space is the
# thing under test. `binary` is `-diff -merge -text`: it keeps any checkout
# from rewriting line endings (the pinned outcomes would then fail for a
# reason that has nothing to do with the reader) and stops `git diff --check`
# from reading that space as whitespace damage.
src-tauri/fuzz/corpus/** binary
